---
/**
 * t67 · Drift
 *
 * A chat bubble is a still object. What is moving across it here is the
 * light.
 *
 * The tone field is a single broad reflection travelling on a shallow
 * diagonal: hard on its leading edge, where the light has just arrived, and
 * smeared for twice as far behind it, where it is leaving. That asymmetry is
 * the whole idea. A symmetric highlight reads as a moulded, static bevel;
 * one with a leading edge and a trailing smear reads as something passing,
 * which is what a stream is.
 *
 * A weak bounce sits opposite it, low and left, so the surface reads as glass
 * rather than as paint, and a one-pixel inner rim picks out the silhouette
 * only on the lit side.
 *
 * The carrier itself is deliberately ordinary: a six-radius rounded bubble
 * with a short stepped tail off the bottom left. Nothing about the outline is
 * asking to be looked at. The shading is measured across the union of body
 * and tail, so the tail is lit by the same pass and is outlined as part of
 * one silhouette rather than stuck on.
 *
 * The face is the family's md/compact/gap-2, unaltered, and the reflection is
 * flattened to one calm tone across it and its margin, so the moving light
 * never runs through the eyes.
 *
 * 10 violet-to-magenta tones.
 */
import MarkFrame from '../MarkFrame.astro';
import { facePathsAt } from '../../../data/mark';

interface Props { size?: number }
const { size = 128 } = Astro.props;
---

<MarkFrame size={size} title="Twozz — Drift">
